  "scientific_summary": "368315 independent adversarial qualification, Claude Opus 5.5: the author theorem r(n) = 1 - O_m(1/n) is correct and independently reconstructed, recommendation EXCLUDE AS ROUTINE OR CORRECTION, moderate confidence. ROOT ADOPTS EXCLUSION, credit 0. Unlike the earlier cases this review supplies a complete reduction to primary statements actually read: on full interval-closed sets whose image is also full, psi(I) = (Delta Ceil(I) union L(I), L(I)) conjugates rowmotion to ordinary rowmotion on J([m]x[n]x[2]); non-full sets and those meeting them number O(n^(2m-1)); rowmotion on that distributive lattice has order m+n+1 by Striker-Williams Theorem 7.5, attributed to Cameron and Fon-Der-Flaass, and Dilks-Pechenik-Striker Corollary 4.5 bounds shorter orbits by O(n^m). The value m+n+1 is the classical order a+b+c-1 at c=2, the noncrossing rotation is already printed as rule (2) of Striker-Williams Definition 7.6, and the source section 4.1 names the plan. Same pattern as 336276. Limits: the conjugacy psi is reviewer-authored and has not been independently reviewed; the 1995 and 2014 originals were not read directly; two searches found no earlier proof, so this is a routine-corollary judgment and not an authenticated prior proof; the user may overrule. Strongest dissent recorded: a deliberate printed conjecture fully proved with a rate, and the conjugacy is in nothing read. The author correctly notes that the source orbit claim as worded fails at m=1, n=6, a correction earning no credit. Disclosed: denial chunks 07-10 were piped through head -c outside the runner and one JSON validity check ran outside the runner.",
